1
00:01:40,763 --> 00:01:42,553
[Episode 9]

2
00:02:04,151 --> 00:02:07,800
Your hands are warm.

3
00:02:09,591 --> 00:02:12,093
Were your hands cold?

4
00:02:12,093 --> 00:02:13,620
No.

5
00:02:18,958 --> 00:02:20,532
Warmer now, isn't it?

6
00:02:39,102 --> 00:02:40,649
I...

7
00:02:41,902 --> 00:02:43,827
wanted to hold your hand so badly,

8
00:02:43,827 --> 00:02:45,794
but do you know how much I held back?

9
00:02:47,433 --> 00:02:51,564
Trying not to cross the line
between a CEO and an employee.

10
00:02:54,251 --> 00:02:56,077
So take responsibility.

11
00:02:57,344 --> 00:02:59,024
Responsibility?

12
00:02:59,024 --> 00:03:03,787
No matter what happens,
don't let go of my hand.

13
00:03:06,745 --> 00:03:08,245
Okay.

14
00:03:11,693 --> 00:03:19,158
But there's already so much gossip,
and if I start dating you...

15
00:03:19,878 --> 00:03:21,805
I know.

16
00:03:21,805 --> 00:03:24,157
Let's keep it a secret at work

17
00:03:24,157 --> 00:03:27,936
and just grow closer for a while,
the two of us.

18
00:03:29,764 --> 00:03:32,081
Thank you for being considerate.

19
00:03:34,438 --> 00:03:35,995
Right.

20
00:03:39,291 --> 00:03:43,575
It's cold, so bundle up on your way.

21
00:03:46,611 --> 00:03:50,097
Sir, get going. I'll head inside.

22
00:03:50,097 --> 00:03:51,658
After I see you go in.

23
00:03:53,748 --> 00:03:56,935
It's cold. I told you to go.

24
00:03:56,935 --> 00:03:58,943
You go in first.

25
00:03:58,943 --> 00:04:02,318
Okay. I'll go.

26
00:04:09,696 --> 00:04:13,050
- You go.
- I'm going.

27
00:04:41,824 --> 00:04:43,698
<i>What are you still doing there?</i>

28
00:04:43,698 --> 00:04:45,183
<i>Hurry up and go.</i>

29
00:04:45,183 --> 00:04:47,922
<i>All right. I'm going.</i>

30
00:05:25,618 --> 00:05:27,982
This is crazy.

31
00:05:35,268 --> 00:05:38,680
[CEO Kang Ha Gi, APPELLO]
<i>Sleep well and see you tomorrow. Sweet dreams.</i>

32
00:05:50,833 --> 00:05:54,016
[Ms. Nam Da Reum]
<i>Sweet dreams to you too, sir.</i>

33
00:06:02,514 --> 00:06:06,571
[Ms. Nam Da Reum]

34
00:06:07,677 --> 00:06:12,076
<i>Sweet dreams to you too, sir.</i>

35
00:06:12,076 --> 00:06:16,930
[Ms. Nam Da Reum]

36
00:06:45,335 --> 00:06:48,585
Nam Da Reum, you've got this!

37
00:07:02,668 --> 00:07:04,417
Hello.

38
00:07:11,347 --> 00:07:13,428
Good morning!

39
00:07:15,590 --> 00:07:17,740
Well, look who it is!

40
00:07:17,740 --> 00:07:19,380
Da Reum!

41
00:07:19,380 --> 00:07:22,900
Da Reum, you're back?

42
00:07:22,900 --> 00:07:26,126
Hello. Hello.

43
00:07:27,563 --> 00:07:30,316
Yes. I reported for work as usual.

44
00:07:30,316 --> 00:07:34,132
- Da Reum, I missed you.
- I missed you too.

45
00:07:34,132 --> 00:07:36,811
- Really.
- Da Reum.

46
00:07:36,811 --> 00:07:40,725
It's so good to have the three of us
together like this.

47
00:07:43,015 --> 00:07:47,672
Nam Da Reum! Welcome to APPELLO!

48
00:07:48,420 --> 00:07:51,461
Hey, remember that?
I blocked the camera for you.

49
00:07:51,461 --> 00:07:52,988
Thank you so much.

50
00:07:52,988 --> 00:07:54,106
It was nothing.

51
00:07:54,106 --> 00:07:55,610
- Really?
- Of course.

52
00:07:55,610 --> 00:07:57,492
- Seriously?
- Seriously.

53
00:07:57,492 --> 00:08:01,306
What happened with your resignation letter?

54
00:08:02,661 --> 00:08:05,777
It was rejected.
You never submitted it for e-approval.

55
00:08:05,777 --> 00:08:08,524
And with no remote request,
it's an unexcused absence.

56
00:08:10,903 --> 00:08:14,218
From now on,
I'll be sure to file through e-approval.

57
00:08:14,218 --> 00:08:19,239
And I'll work overtime to make up
for every day I missed, if I have to.

58
00:08:20,977 --> 00:08:22,597
Well...

59
00:08:23,213 --> 00:08:25,268
Follow the process, please.

60
00:08:26,374 --> 00:08:27,668
Get back to work.

61
00:08:27,668 --> 00:08:29,622
- Yes, understood.
- Yes, sir!

62
00:08:29,622 --> 00:08:32,468
- Process.
- Congratulations. Congratulations.

63
00:08:32,468 --> 00:08:33,862
Process.

64
00:08:33,862 --> 00:08:36,035
What a relief.

65
00:08:36,035 --> 00:08:41,515
Da Reum, he might sound like that,
but he was really worried about you.

66
00:09:23,591 --> 00:09:26,660
[CEO Kang Ha Gi, APPELLO]
<i>Did you get in okay? Meet me in the storeroom.</i>

67
00:09:28,555 --> 00:09:31,030
- Hello.
- Hello.

68
00:09:40,741 --> 00:09:42,158
This is it.

69
00:09:47,841 --> 00:09:50,845
But where is he?

70
00:10:00,915 --> 00:10:03,709
Did you sleep well last night?

71
00:10:05,141 --> 00:10:06,615
Yes.

72
00:10:11,260 --> 00:10:13,222
It's fine. There's no one here.

73
00:10:13,222 --> 00:10:15,967
What if someone sees us?

74
00:10:15,967 --> 00:10:19,444
I just wanted to talk for a bit.

75
00:10:24,249 --> 00:10:29,601
This won't work. Let's make some rules.

76
00:10:29,601 --> 00:10:31,915
Rules?

77
00:10:31,915 --> 00:10:34,727
Rules for our secret office romance.

78
00:10:53,513 --> 00:10:56,736
First, no physical contact at work.

79
00:10:56,736 --> 00:10:58,025
[1. No physical contact at work]

80
00:11:00,994 --> 00:11:05,333
Especially in front of people.
Not even standing next to me.

81
00:11:05,947 --> 00:11:06,958
Second.

82
00:11:06,958 --> 00:11:09,756
- Let's begin the meeting.
- Yes.

83
00:11:14,264 --> 00:11:17,531
[Seoul Night View Date Spots]

84
00:11:19,590 --> 00:11:22,278
No letting on that we're dating.

85
00:11:22,278 --> 00:11:24,221
[2. No letting on that we're dating]

86
00:11:24,221 --> 00:11:25,406
[Seoul Night View Date Spots]

87
00:11:39,266 --> 00:11:42,572
Be careful not to start office gossip.

88
00:11:42,572 --> 00:11:44,033
Careful again.

89
00:11:45,228 --> 00:11:47,008
Third.

90
00:11:53,448 --> 00:11:55,390
[CEO Kang Ha Gi, APPELLO]
<i>I miss you.</i>

91
00:11:58,041 --> 00:12:00,946
[Team Lead Choi Seong Wook]
<i>What do you mean, sir?</i>

92
00:12:03,430 --> 00:12:06,030
[APPELLO Internal Announcements]

93
00:12:17,101 --> 00:12:19,530
[CEO Kang Ha Gi, APPELLO]
<i>Next year's business plan.</i>

94
00:12:22,739 --> 00:12:25,414
Private conversations by message only.

95
00:12:25,414 --> 00:12:30,121
Actually, no messages at work either,
in case we mix up the chat rooms.

96
00:12:30,121 --> 00:12:32,244
[3. No messages at work either]

97
00:12:34,763 --> 00:12:39,717
And if you startle people like this...

98
00:12:40,496 --> 00:12:42,102
That's a penalty point.

99
00:12:43,049 --> 00:12:44,300
A penalty point?

100
00:12:44,300 --> 00:12:45,386
Yes.

101
00:12:45,386 --> 00:12:50,182
Whoever racks up penalty points
buys the meals and the coffee.

102
00:12:50,182 --> 00:12:53,394
I won't even make eye contact at work.

103
00:12:55,722 --> 00:12:57,892
That's a bit harsh, isn't it?

104
00:12:57,892 --> 00:13:00,412
That's why I'm telling you to be careful.

105
00:13:00,412 --> 00:13:05,227
This feels a bit unfair.
There should be a reward, too.

106
00:13:06,020 --> 00:13:10,399
That's just how it works.

107
00:13:15,155 --> 00:13:17,750
Why am I the only one...

108
00:13:18,794 --> 00:13:20,884
Penalty points...

109
00:13:21,688 --> 00:13:23,942
You're not just asking me to be careful...

110
00:13:30,472 --> 00:13:34,720
This is an exception.

111
00:13:38,889 --> 00:13:40,836
An exception...

112
00:13:40,836 --> 00:13:42,807
Thank you.

113
00:13:47,011 --> 00:13:48,061
Da Reum!

114
00:13:48,061 --> 00:13:51,648
- Team Lead Kim needs the sample now. Found it?
- What? Yes.

115
00:13:51,648 --> 00:13:54,777
- I'll bring it right now!
- Okay.

116
00:13:54,777 --> 00:13:56,290
Go on.

117
00:14:00,679 --> 00:14:02,223
Wait...

118
00:14:06,094 --> 00:14:08,027
What's with her today?

119
00:14:12,700 --> 00:14:15,445
[APPELLO X Im Cheong Rim]

120
00:14:15,445 --> 00:14:17,671
[Knot keyring DIY Kit Experience Zone]

121
00:14:17,671 --> 00:14:19,628
[UNFRAMED: Untying Tradition, Knotting It Anew]

122
00:14:32,636 --> 00:14:34,724
Da Reum!

123
00:14:34,724 --> 00:14:36,868
You're here!

124
00:14:36,868 --> 00:14:41,023
It looks even better than I imagined.

125
00:14:41,643 --> 00:14:43,756
Master Im!

126
00:14:44,970 --> 00:14:48,150
You worked so hard getting this ready.

127
00:14:49,161 --> 00:14:52,973
Not at all. I had so much fun preparing it.

128
00:14:55,022 --> 00:14:58,076
Apparently if you'd dropped out,
Master Im would have quit too.

129
00:14:58,076 --> 00:14:59,537
Stop that.

130
00:15:02,777 --> 00:15:05,395
You saw the article, right?

131
00:15:05,395 --> 00:15:07,931
I saw it.

132
00:15:07,931 --> 00:15:14,131
But no matter what others say,
I know how you work.

133
00:15:16,423 --> 00:15:18,469
Thank you, Master Im.

134
00:15:21,056 --> 00:15:23,734
So, what should I get ready now?

135
00:15:24,801 --> 00:15:28,383
Later, could I ask you to run one rehearsal
with Director Lee over there?

136
00:15:28,383 --> 00:15:31,000
- With Director Lee?
- Yes.

137
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,655
Master Im!

138
00:15:33,350 --> 00:15:35,003
Master Im.

139
00:15:35,003 --> 00:15:37,601
- Shall we head over there?
- Yes.

140
00:15:57,063 --> 00:15:59,015
Hello, Director Lee.

141
00:16:01,073 --> 00:16:02,815
Hello.

142
00:16:25,050 --> 00:16:26,714
Have you been well?

143
00:16:28,648 --> 00:16:30,225
Yes.

144
00:16:36,703 --> 00:16:38,805
Director Lee.

145
00:16:39,609 --> 00:16:42,996
Could I see you for a moment after the event?

146
00:17:09,343 --> 00:17:13,698
If you tuck it in this way,
the whole thing comes together.

147
00:17:20,675 --> 00:17:23,753
Do it like this, and the first knot is done.

148
00:17:23,753 --> 00:17:28,291
What I'm making now is a Dongsimgyeol.
It means one heart.

149
00:17:28,291 --> 00:17:31,909
Now if you pull this side a little tighter...

150
00:17:44,749 --> 00:17:46,649
It came out crooked.

151
00:17:51,328 --> 00:17:53,621
It came undone. One moment.

152
00:17:54,536 --> 00:17:56,026
You see?

153
00:17:56,640 --> 00:18:01,015
If you pull only one side hard, like I did,
the knot comes out crooked.

154
00:18:01,015 --> 00:18:07,354
You get the most beautiful knot
when both sides pull with equal force.

155
00:18:07,354 --> 00:18:09,951
- Like this.
- It's so pretty.

156
00:18:28,150 --> 00:18:29,798
Good work today.

157
00:18:29,798 --> 00:18:31,782
The Dongsimgyeol explanation was good.

158
00:18:31,782 --> 00:18:33,699
The customers responded well, too.

159
00:18:34,816 --> 00:18:36,919
You look pretty happy.

160
00:18:37,970 --> 00:18:41,992
The boycott's died down, Da Reum's back,

161
00:18:42,790 --> 00:18:44,603
your gamble paid off.

162
00:18:51,337 --> 00:18:52,791
Chan.

163
00:18:53,718 --> 00:18:58,133
I'm going to be more honest with you now.

164
00:19:00,457 --> 00:19:02,460
The truth is...

165
00:19:03,990 --> 00:19:06,145
I don't think I need to hear it.

166
00:19:09,503 --> 00:19:14,047
Come to think of it,
the things you never told me all this time

167
00:19:14,047 --> 00:19:16,696
were things that would hurt to hear.

168
00:19:17,904 --> 00:19:21,497
So I won't hear it this time either.

169
00:19:47,437 --> 00:19:49,217
Oppa.

170
00:19:59,471 --> 00:20:01,139
Congratulations on your return.

171
00:20:02,190 --> 00:20:03,923
It was hard, wasn't it?

172
00:20:06,104 --> 00:20:07,783
Not really.

173
00:20:08,738 --> 00:20:11,101
You must have had a hard time too, oppa.

174
00:20:13,404 --> 00:20:16,997
I was a bit of a wreck.

175
00:20:18,437 --> 00:20:20,380
I felt like I failed to protect you.

176
00:20:28,751 --> 00:20:30,831
You did protect me.

177
00:20:31,923 --> 00:20:34,213
You even did an interview because of me.

178
00:20:37,650 --> 00:20:39,706
I'm grateful you see it that way.

179
00:20:45,017 --> 00:20:50,017
Oppa, is work all right?

180
00:20:50,017 --> 00:20:51,877
The movie?

181
00:20:54,424 --> 00:20:56,691
I didn't get fired.

182
00:20:56,691 --> 00:20:58,959
What a relief.

183
00:21:00,331 --> 00:21:03,711
Bad press and getting bashed is nothing new.

184
00:21:03,711 --> 00:21:05,200
I'm used to it.

185
00:21:10,230 --> 00:21:14,150
Since it's come to this,
let's meet openly from now on.

186
00:21:15,083 --> 00:21:16,703
Pardon?

187
00:21:16,703 --> 00:21:19,206
As a fan, a friend, whatever.

188
00:21:20,710 --> 00:21:23,343
I want you to stay by my side.

189
00:21:29,911 --> 00:21:32,091
Oppa...

190
00:21:32,091 --> 00:21:35,662
you're someone very precious to me.

191
00:21:36,677 --> 00:21:39,966
That sounds a lot like past tense.

192
00:21:39,966 --> 00:21:43,386
No. You're precious to me now, too.

193
00:21:47,424 --> 00:21:49,433
- But...
- It's okay.

194
00:21:50,258 --> 00:21:52,356
Even if there's someone more precious.

195
00:21:56,803 --> 00:21:58,393
Just...

196
00:21:59,624 --> 00:22:02,154
as long as you're smiling,
that's enough for me.

197
00:22:03,438 --> 00:22:05,407
Just stay by my side.

198
00:22:39,597 --> 00:22:43,689
<i>I want to give us a real shot, Da Reum.</i>

199
00:22:43,689 --> 00:22:47,349
<i>I don't think you're someone I could love,</i>

200
00:22:47,349 --> 00:22:51,303
<i>but someone I still look up to, like an idol.</i>

201
00:23:16,798 --> 00:23:19,445
[Ha Gi]

202
00:23:48,881 --> 00:23:51,574
- Thank you.
- Thank you. Thank you.

203
00:23:51,574 --> 00:23:53,536
Thank you, have a great day!

204
00:23:53,536 --> 00:23:57,337
Yes, welcome.

205
00:23:58,718 --> 00:24:03,010
This is the list of brands that recently
ended their exclusive contracts with us.

206
00:24:04,617 --> 00:24:08,935
Next is the list of new brands SE:ON announced.

207
00:24:08,935 --> 00:24:11,084
Comparing the two lists...

208
00:24:16,424 --> 00:24:21,719
As you can see, most exclusive brands that left
show a confirmed pattern of moving to SE.

209
00:24:21,719 --> 00:24:24,793
- Look at that, they took them all.
- I told you there's a mole.

210
00:24:24,793 --> 00:24:27,578
We have to find them. This makes no sense.

211
00:24:41,319 --> 00:24:43,667
Our job now isn't to suspect each other.

212
00:24:43,667 --> 00:24:46,797
It's to stay the number one fashion platform.

213
00:24:48,708 --> 00:24:53,679
SE will only get more aggressive,
and if we just defend, the game goes to them.

214
00:24:53,679 --> 00:24:57,459
From now on, we fight to take from them.

215
00:24:59,983 --> 00:25:01,922
HAN.

216
00:25:01,922 --> 00:25:03,608
HAN?

217
00:25:03,608 --> 00:25:06,378
It's the hottest issue in fashion right now.

218
00:25:11,815 --> 00:25:17,113
Sir, HAN is the hardest brand to get
in the Paris fashion scene.

219
00:25:17,113 --> 00:25:21,337
You're saying SE wants to collaborate
with HAN?

220
00:25:21,337 --> 00:25:24,015
This is huge, isn't it?

221
00:25:24,015 --> 00:25:27,405
The way to turn this crisis around...

222
00:25:28,509 --> 00:25:30,510
is for us to bring HAN in.

223
00:25:35,295 --> 00:25:40,680
I'm forming a dedicated task force,
so anyone can sign up.

224
00:25:42,049 --> 00:25:44,795
This isn't going to be easy.

225
00:25:57,124 --> 00:25:58,604
[Pop-up Event Results Report]

226
00:26:43,381 --> 00:26:46,938
<i>I've emailed you the log records
and the CCTV captures.</i>

227
00:26:58,683 --> 00:27:00,568
Jackpot! This is a huge one.

228
00:27:00,568 --> 00:27:03,188
I just heard in the security room...

229
00:27:03,188 --> 00:27:04,977
What? What?

230
00:27:09,457 --> 00:27:12,250
- Is that Hye Soo?
- Yeah.

231
00:27:12,250 --> 00:27:13,950
Is that really her?

232
00:27:17,249 --> 00:27:18,906
Ms. Seo.

233
00:27:18,906 --> 00:27:21,965
You know external email is banned
at the office, right?

234
00:27:22,669 --> 00:27:23,671
Yes.

235
00:27:23,671 --> 00:27:26,104
Then why did you break the security rules?

236
00:27:27,982 --> 00:27:30,353
I don't quite remember...

237
00:27:31,089 --> 00:27:34,032
But why are you asking?

238
00:27:42,789 --> 00:27:45,097
This is...

239
00:27:47,698 --> 00:27:52,292
Don't tell me you suspect I'm the spy?

240
00:27:54,037 --> 00:27:55,613
It's absolutely not me.

241
00:27:55,613 --> 00:27:57,957
Me, a spy? That's ridiculous.

242
00:27:57,957 --> 00:28:03,138
Spy or not, this dating rumor photo
looks like your work, Ms. Seo.

243
00:28:19,368 --> 00:28:21,299
<i>I came to give you this.</i>

244
00:28:25,215 --> 00:28:26,725
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

245
00:28:31,103 --> 00:28:34,770
<i>Sir, could I ask you to check this?</i>

246
00:28:34,770 --> 00:28:38,396
You turned down my confession on the spot.

247
00:28:42,910 --> 00:28:44,641
<i>- Why?
- You don't need it?</i>

248
00:28:44,641 --> 00:28:47,220
<i>Then could I have one...</i>

249
00:28:49,222 --> 00:28:53,880
But I got angry
when I saw you meeting Da Reum alone.

250
00:28:56,645 --> 00:29:00,159
A reporter gave me a business card, so...

251
00:29:01,997 --> 00:29:03,942
I had no idea it would blow up like this.

252
00:29:03,942 --> 00:29:05,836
Ms. Seo.

253
00:29:05,836 --> 00:29:09,129
Do you know how much damage
this has done to the company?

254
00:29:10,396 --> 00:29:11,993
I'm so sorry.

255
00:29:13,203 --> 00:29:17,372
You'll be disciplined under company policy.

256
00:29:18,763 --> 00:29:24,614
And think carefully about
who really deserves an apology.

257
00:30:34,369 --> 00:30:36,767
Thank you.

258
00:30:36,767 --> 00:30:38,907
I should be the grateful one.

259
00:30:42,482 --> 00:30:45,190
I found it thanks to your tip-off.

260
00:30:45,929 --> 00:30:50,076
I am a walking dashcam, after all.

261
00:30:51,286 --> 00:30:54,486
But Ms. Seo isn't the spy.
She only leaked the photos.

262
00:30:54,486 --> 00:30:59,269
Really? Then who's the real spy?

263
00:31:01,172 --> 00:31:04,829
Anyway, thank you.

264
00:31:10,559 --> 00:31:14,828
Sir, I'll keep my eyes peeled.

265
00:31:26,694 --> 00:31:28,258
Seriously.

266
00:31:28,258 --> 00:31:31,642
I came to deliver chicken,
not to take out the trash.

267
00:31:31,642 --> 00:31:36,553
Where on earth did Roy oppa go?

268
00:31:40,355 --> 00:31:44,046
Do you even watch where you're going?

269
00:31:44,046 --> 00:31:45,886
Are you okay?

270
00:31:47,073 --> 00:31:49,145
<i>That voice...</i>

271
00:31:49,145 --> 00:31:50,920
Are you badly hurt?

272
00:31:50,920 --> 00:31:52,640
<i>Roy?</i>

273
00:31:55,779 --> 00:31:58,592
I'm dying. My back!

274
00:31:58,592 --> 00:32:00,483
My backside!

275
00:32:01,288 --> 00:32:05,292
You hit me and won't even show your face.
Is this a hit-and-run?

276
00:32:05,292 --> 00:32:08,692
A hit-and-run? No, it isn't.

277
00:32:08,692 --> 00:32:13,453
Then take off the helmet and apologize.

278
00:32:19,339 --> 00:32:24,059
<i>Take it off. Take it off. Please, take it off!</i>

279
00:32:42,405 --> 00:32:46,751
I'm sorry. I was careless. I'm sorry.

280
00:32:47,382 --> 00:32:48,835
Excuse me...

281
00:33:00,292 --> 00:33:01,985
Yes.

282
00:33:01,985 --> 00:33:03,478
Yes.

283
00:33:09,105 --> 00:33:11,401
Is it that bad? Should we go to the ER?

284
00:33:11,401 --> 00:33:14,311
No. No, I'm fine.

285
00:33:14,311 --> 00:33:16,091
- Are you okay?
- Yes.

286
00:33:18,593 --> 00:33:20,792
- Now let go of my hand...
- Yes.

287
00:33:26,370 --> 00:33:29,416
This brand called HAN is really fascinating.

288
00:33:29,416 --> 00:33:31,964
They don't even disclose
who the creative director is.

289
00:33:31,964 --> 00:33:34,759
On social media, there's only a brand account.

290
00:33:34,759 --> 00:33:37,949
That actually makes me more curious.

291
00:33:39,163 --> 00:33:41,854
Let's stop here and eat first. I'm hungry.

292
00:33:41,854 --> 00:33:43,856
- Sounds good.
- Sounds good.

293
00:33:43,856 --> 00:33:47,325
Everyone, you see this?
What do you think this is?

294
00:33:47,325 --> 00:33:50,877
Behold, in my hand is the company card!

295
00:33:50,877 --> 00:33:53,341
What do you want to eat?
What do you want to eat?

296
00:33:53,341 --> 00:33:54,731
- Army stew.
- Army stew?

297
00:33:54,731 --> 00:33:58,734
Let's eat first. Let's go! Follow me.
Army stew? What else?

298
00:33:58,734 --> 00:34:02,230
- Let's grill steak!
- Stir-fried octopus, stir-fried octopus.

299
00:34:09,199 --> 00:34:10,257
Da Reum, you coming?

300
00:34:10,257 --> 00:34:12,160
Yes. I'm coming.

301
00:34:34,839 --> 00:34:36,364
I know...

302
00:34:36,364 --> 00:34:39,157
- She had it coming.
- Exactly.

303
00:34:49,720 --> 00:34:53,942
Ms. Seo, could I speak with you a moment?

304
00:34:56,861 --> 00:34:58,494
Yeah.

305
00:35:03,019 --> 00:35:05,715
- What's going on?
- Are they going to fight?

306
00:35:18,459 --> 00:35:20,779
Ms. Seo.

307
00:35:20,779 --> 00:35:22,608
What?

308
00:35:26,640 --> 00:35:29,297
What is this? You want to actually throw down?

309
00:35:31,299 --> 00:35:35,446
Wait, wait. I'm sorry.
I'm really sorry. I'm really sorry.

310
00:35:49,039 --> 00:35:52,098
Don't you have something to say to me?

311
00:35:56,532 --> 00:35:57,962
I'm sorry.

312
00:36:00,133 --> 00:36:02,385
I said I'm really sorry.

313
00:36:03,326 --> 00:36:04,862
I must have been crazy.

314
00:36:06,906 --> 00:36:09,997
Thanks to you, I had to write an apology letter

315
00:36:10,839 --> 00:36:12,959
and got frozen out. Can't you see?

316
00:36:13,719 --> 00:36:17,268
I know I did something worth punishing,

317
00:36:18,366 --> 00:36:20,990
but it's so hard I want to quit right now.

318
00:36:22,832 --> 00:36:24,946
I know.

319
00:36:24,946 --> 00:36:26,970
I got through it alone, too.

320
00:36:29,139 --> 00:36:33,540
If we don't sort this out,
it'll keep being hard for you.

321
00:36:35,792 --> 00:36:43,149
So what, are you being the bigger person
and forgiving me?

322
00:36:43,846 --> 00:36:45,356
Not yet.

323
00:36:46,413 --> 00:36:51,602
But I'm still offering my hand.

324
00:36:52,946 --> 00:36:58,812
If you're really sorry, then help me out.

325
00:37:03,696 --> 00:37:06,329
What am I supposed to do...

326
00:37:06,329 --> 00:37:09,347
I'm having a hard time writing
the HAN task force proposal.

327
00:37:09,347 --> 00:37:11,729
You've done a lot of these, haven't you?

328
00:37:12,476 --> 00:37:14,750
Let's do it together.

329
00:37:17,515 --> 00:37:19,384
- Together?
- Yeah.

330
00:37:24,283 --> 00:37:26,115
Fine, whatever.

331
00:38:04,693 --> 00:38:07,495
Welcome. Take your time looking around.

332
00:38:10,416 --> 00:38:13,453
Who directs this store?

333
00:38:13,453 --> 00:38:17,243
Our Director Lee Chan.

334
00:38:20,129 --> 00:38:21,407
I'll take this one.

335
00:38:21,407 --> 00:38:24,499
Yes, I'll ring you up over there.

336
00:38:45,509 --> 00:38:48,557
[Ha Gi]
<i>Let's talk. Stop avoiding me.</i>

337
00:38:59,096 --> 00:39:01,859
Lee Chan, is that you?

338
00:39:06,442 --> 00:39:07,893
Jeong Yeon sunbae?

339
00:39:09,469 --> 00:39:11,495
- I'll see you next time.
- Yes.

340
00:39:14,836 --> 00:39:16,976
It really is you.

341
00:39:21,349 --> 00:39:23,375
When did you get back to Korea?

342
00:39:24,922 --> 00:39:27,296
Just a few days ago.

343
00:39:27,296 --> 00:39:30,978
It's been almost 15 years, hasn't it?

344
00:39:32,343 --> 00:39:34,655
You never once got in touch.

345
00:39:36,163 --> 00:39:38,094
So you did miss me?

346
00:39:42,902 --> 00:39:47,449
This brings back memories.
Those were good days.

347
00:39:47,449 --> 00:39:50,549
Listening to music with you at school.

348
00:39:51,676 --> 00:39:52,834
Remember?

349
00:39:52,834 --> 00:39:58,887
We said at 20 we'd hear live music
at a jazz bar and try whiskey together.

350
00:39:58,887 --> 00:40:01,525
But you weren't there at 20.

351
00:40:05,402 --> 00:40:07,237
I'm sorry about that.

352
00:40:09,436 --> 00:40:11,951
I did miss you two, though.

353
00:40:14,223 --> 00:40:15,753
Us two?

354
00:40:16,510 --> 00:40:18,110
You and Ha Gi.

355
00:40:22,943 --> 00:40:24,777
Is Ha Gi doing well?

356
00:40:25,529 --> 00:40:27,810
You two were always together.

357
00:40:28,476 --> 00:40:31,289
You really haven't changed, sunbae.

358
00:40:31,289 --> 00:40:32,328
What hasn't?

359
00:40:32,328 --> 00:40:34,518
Making people uncomfortable.

360
00:40:38,542 --> 00:40:43,918
I thought being a celebrity made you cooler,
but you haven't changed either.

361
00:40:49,416 --> 00:40:52,952
I'm staying at the boutique just up the street.

362
00:40:53,662 --> 00:40:55,615
Let's meet again soon.

363
00:41:15,356 --> 00:41:20,383
You're really good with a knife.

364
00:41:20,383 --> 00:41:24,647
They used to call me the Blade of Seocho.

365
00:41:27,029 --> 00:41:29,785
Back then, the smell of blood...

366
00:41:33,479 --> 00:41:37,029
The Blade?

367
00:41:37,029 --> 00:41:41,409
That's all in the past.
Now I'm the neighborhood punching bag.

368
00:41:42,390 --> 00:41:45,872
<i>He doesn't have a criminal record, does he?</i>

369
00:41:45,872 --> 00:41:49,245
So Mi Mi, what's your ideal type?

370
00:41:51,096 --> 00:41:53,499
My ideal type? My ideal type?

371
00:41:54,090 --> 00:41:59,352
I like a man who's successful...
and a good kisser?

372
00:42:05,972 --> 00:42:08,621
Very clear answer.

373
00:42:08,621 --> 00:42:10,046
That's exactly me.

374
00:42:18,326 --> 00:42:20,714
I'll just run to the restroom.

375
00:42:20,714 --> 00:42:22,519
Of course, of course.

376
00:42:34,462 --> 00:42:36,165
My heart's racing.

377
00:42:37,855 --> 00:42:40,504
A kiss today, too?

378
00:42:41,558 --> 00:42:43,546
Isn't that moving too fast?

379
00:42:44,190 --> 00:42:46,407
Not successful, either.

380
00:42:48,303 --> 00:42:50,272
And probably not a good kisser.

381
00:42:57,333 --> 00:42:59,565
Yeah, so?

382
00:43:00,383 --> 00:43:02,059
No knife prepared.

383
00:43:03,182 --> 00:43:05,862
Should we start with abduction and confinement?

384
00:43:05,862 --> 00:43:07,683
Murder might be pushing it.

385
00:43:09,788 --> 00:43:11,939
It's borderline.

386
00:43:13,792 --> 00:43:18,206
Something urgent came up,
so I'll head off first.

387
00:43:18,206 --> 00:43:20,715
Mi Mi! Mi Mi!

388
00:43:22,123 --> 00:43:24,399
Mi Mi, wait a moment!

389
00:43:24,399 --> 00:43:26,955
Why are you following me? It's scary!

390
00:43:26,955 --> 00:43:29,213
What's wrong with her? Mi Mi!

391
00:43:38,617 --> 00:43:40,512
- Please help me!
- Why, what's the matter?

392
00:43:40,512 --> 00:43:43,015
Someone's chasing me.

393
00:43:45,307 --> 00:43:47,124
My stomach hurts.

394
00:43:48,300 --> 00:43:50,973
Take your coat. Your coat.

395
00:43:53,678 --> 00:43:55,187
[Lawyer Kim Min Woo]

396
00:44:00,810 --> 00:44:05,086
I don't know what you misunderstood,
but I really am a lawyer.

397
00:44:05,086 --> 00:44:07,198
You know what shape I'm in, Mi Mi.

398
00:44:07,198 --> 00:44:09,834
Would a gangster have a hunched neck,

399
00:44:09,834 --> 00:44:12,324
rounded shoulders and a slipped disc?

400
00:44:12,324 --> 00:44:14,824
Why didn't you say so from the start?

401
00:44:14,824 --> 00:44:17,013
You never asked.

402
00:44:17,013 --> 00:44:22,235
It looks cheap to push my job
when nobody even asked.

403
00:44:41,538 --> 00:44:43,188
Min Ah, one moment.

404
00:44:46,568 --> 00:44:52,588
Ms. Seo, I drafted it like this for now.
What do you think?

405
00:44:57,414 --> 00:44:58,993
Let's see...

406
00:44:58,993 --> 00:45:04,699
The first page decides the company's image,
and this is too plain.

407
00:45:04,699 --> 00:45:07,560
Always lead with the conclusion.

408
00:45:08,605 --> 00:45:10,419
Then...

409
00:45:20,583 --> 00:45:23,430
You two are working hard together.

410
00:45:29,214 --> 00:45:32,176
This one, then this one, like that.

411
00:45:32,176 --> 00:45:33,477
- 3, 1, 2?
- Yeah, yeah.

412
00:45:33,477 --> 00:45:34,922
Yes.

413
00:45:55,794 --> 00:45:58,535
All right, let's call it a day.

414
00:45:58,535 --> 00:45:59,900
- Especially marketing.
- Sorry?

415
00:45:59,900 --> 00:46:01,605
It's late. Why aren't you leaving?

416
00:46:01,605 --> 00:46:04,333
I still have work left.

417
00:46:08,775 --> 00:46:11,027
The direction's good. Just fix the details.

418
00:46:11,027 --> 00:46:13,267
Do it tomorrow. Rest is part of the job.

419
00:46:13,267 --> 00:46:14,461
Go home, now.

420
00:46:14,461 --> 00:46:16,902
Sir, just one look at my proposal too...

421
00:46:21,581 --> 00:46:23,875
- Go home, now.
- What? Is it that perfect?

422
00:46:23,875 --> 00:46:26,437
This won't be done today. Redo it tomorrow.

423
00:46:27,330 --> 00:46:31,855
Come on, off you go. Hurry up. Quickly.

424
00:46:31,855 --> 00:46:33,031
- Yes.
- Go on.

425
00:46:33,031 --> 00:46:34,297
Let's go, marketing team.

426
00:46:34,297 --> 00:46:35,411
- Go on. Go on.
- Yes.

427
00:46:35,411 --> 00:46:36,715
Go on. Go on, hurry.

428
00:46:36,715 --> 00:46:39,053
- Yes, good work today.
- Let's go.

429
00:47:11,704 --> 00:47:14,011
Sir, you're not much of a cook, are you?

430
00:47:16,415 --> 00:47:19,775
Well, that's right. Not really...

431
00:47:19,775 --> 00:47:23,552
I may not be good at much,
but I make really good pasta.

432
00:47:24,641 --> 00:47:26,188
Really?

433
00:47:26,188 --> 00:47:30,679
I just heat the sauce I bought
and add the noodles.

434
00:47:46,775 --> 00:47:50,193
Ms. Nam, shall we switch?

435
00:47:50,193 --> 00:47:51,415
Why?

436
00:47:51,415 --> 00:47:53,977
I'm a bit clumsy with a knife.

437
00:47:55,268 --> 00:47:57,174
Move aside. I'll do it.

438
00:48:43,925 --> 00:48:45,252
It's delicious.

439
00:48:45,252 --> 00:48:46,888
Ms. Nam, you really do make good pasta.

440
00:48:46,888 --> 00:48:50,569
Right? I told you I'm good.

441
00:48:50,569 --> 00:48:53,305
Next time, I'll invite you to my place.

442
00:48:53,955 --> 00:48:56,306
To your place?

443
00:48:57,241 --> 00:49:01,564
The second thing I make well is tteokbokki.

444
00:49:01,564 --> 00:49:03,520
Let's make it together.

445
00:49:05,874 --> 00:49:07,743
Yes, let's.

446
00:49:22,571 --> 00:49:27,360
But you knew it was Ms. Seo.

447
00:49:28,252 --> 00:49:29,940
Why didn't you say anything?

448
00:49:35,211 --> 00:49:38,930
I didn't want to suspect her carelessly.

449
00:49:39,885 --> 00:49:44,688
There were plenty of other people
who could have helped with the proposal.

450
00:49:45,958 --> 00:49:48,135
I told you before, didn't I?

451
00:49:49,325 --> 00:49:50,926
That I was bullied.

452
00:49:55,085 --> 00:50:00,872
Looking at Ms. Seo,
I wondered how much it must hurt...

453
00:50:03,618 --> 00:50:05,658
how lonely she must be...

454
00:50:07,838 --> 00:50:10,190
That's what came to mind first.

455
00:50:11,558 --> 00:50:13,300
I didn't want to see...

456
00:50:16,444 --> 00:50:18,634
that version of myself again.

457
00:50:19,765 --> 00:50:21,537
Ms. Nam, you really...

458
00:50:23,052 --> 00:50:28,171
carry your own wounds and still
choose to embrace other people.

459
00:50:33,238 --> 00:50:36,813
You did the same for me, sir.

460
00:50:43,525 --> 00:50:45,271
Actually...

461
00:50:46,450 --> 00:50:48,544
I've lived the opposite way until now.

462
00:50:49,877 --> 00:50:52,949
I tried hard not to get close to anyone.

463
00:50:54,478 --> 00:50:56,905
When I let someone matter to me...

464
00:51:01,685 --> 00:51:03,487
they all left.

465
00:51:05,071 --> 00:51:10,924
It was easier to just work.

466
00:51:13,174 --> 00:51:17,446
But you broke right through that, Ms. Nam.

467
00:51:41,125 --> 00:51:44,471
Do you remember this wine?

468
00:51:44,471 --> 00:51:48,620
Yes. This is the wine I gave you as a gift.

469
00:51:50,004 --> 00:51:54,147
The wine that makes love come true.

470
00:51:59,218 --> 00:52:00,924
So it really was?

471
00:52:21,629 --> 00:52:24,092
[Ha Gi]
[Pick up the phone]

472
00:52:55,113 --> 00:52:58,045
[Kang Ha Gi, APPELLO]

473
00:53:04,593 --> 00:53:07,077
[Dating rumors: CEO Kang's leadership in focus]

474
00:53:51,171 --> 00:53:53,122
Why was it Ha Gi back then?

475
00:53:55,351 --> 00:53:57,004
What was?

476
00:53:57,004 --> 00:53:58,982
The one you chose, sunbae.

477
00:54:01,284 --> 00:54:03,633
Why Kang Ha Gi and not me?

478
00:54:12,451 --> 00:54:14,499
We were first.

479
00:55:15,945 --> 00:55:20,004
In meeting each other, in sharing our hearts.

480
00:55:20,004 --> 00:55:21,578
<i>Min Woo!</i>

481
00:55:41,092 --> 00:55:45,729
When you smiled, sunbae,
I thought it was because of me.

482
00:56:00,927 --> 00:56:02,618
But...

483
00:56:03,889 --> 00:56:06,686
why was it Kang Ha Gi in the end?

484
00:56:17,173 --> 00:56:19,073
Tell me.

485
00:56:21,602 --> 00:56:25,901
That look in your eyes is the same as then.

486
00:56:29,723 --> 00:56:32,629
You always wanted to rescue me.

487
00:56:33,982 --> 00:56:36,155
I was grateful for that...

488
00:56:36,995 --> 00:56:38,748
but I also hated it.

489
00:56:44,457 --> 00:56:46,087
Why?

490
00:56:46,813 --> 00:56:48,749
It felt like pity.

491
00:56:49,555 --> 00:56:51,775
You looked at me like I was pitiful.

492
00:56:53,382 --> 00:56:55,280
Ha Gi wasn't like that.

493
00:56:57,922 --> 00:56:59,718
Back then, he...

494
00:57:01,108 --> 00:57:03,384
just liked me for me.

495
00:57:04,182 --> 00:57:06,358
So I felt at ease, too.

496
00:57:10,709 --> 00:57:12,811
<i>I thought that with someone I like,</i>

497
00:57:12,811 --> 00:57:16,319
<i>I'd laugh and cry,</i>

498
00:57:16,319 --> 00:57:20,145
<i>complain and even get angry,</i>

499
00:57:20,989 --> 00:57:24,229
<i>and I could share my feelings.</i>

500
00:57:24,229 --> 00:57:26,833
<i>But the thing is...</i>

501
00:57:28,162 --> 00:57:30,076
<i>with you, oppa...</i>

502
00:57:30,676 --> 00:57:33,226
<i>I don't think that happened.</i>

503
00:57:46,110 --> 00:57:49,937
Did something happen with Ha Gi?

504
00:57:57,389 --> 00:58:02,322
I shouldn't have come. Take care.

505
00:58:02,322 --> 00:58:03,962
Chan.

506
00:58:09,062 --> 00:58:11,014
Anything I can do to help?

507
00:58:37,268 --> 00:58:39,374
Then try shaking him up.

508
00:58:39,374 --> 00:58:40,887
Kang Ha Gi.

509
00:59:10,304 --> 00:59:12,695
[SE:ON X HAN, Switching Fashion ON]

510
00:59:12,695 --> 00:59:17,219
They never even contacted us,
but they met with SE?

511
00:59:18,281 --> 00:59:20,632
That ship's sailed. It's sailed.

512
00:59:29,411 --> 00:59:30,818
[SE:ON X HAN, Switching Fashion ON]

513
00:59:30,818 --> 00:59:32,939
[HAN made not a brand, but an aesthetic]

514
00:59:37,338 --> 00:59:39,487
Shall I take you to the hotel now?

515
00:59:39,487 --> 00:59:40,990
No.

516
00:59:40,990 --> 00:59:43,817
There's one more place I want to see.

517
00:59:51,315 --> 00:59:54,286
Sir, sir!

518
00:59:54,286 --> 00:59:58,010
The CEO of HAN says they'll visit APPELLO.

519
00:59:58,010 --> 01:00:00,258
- What?
- HAN, I said HAN!

520
01:00:00,258 --> 01:00:02,248
They're on their way. Right now.

521
01:00:20,199 --> 01:00:22,902
They're here? Are they here?

522
01:01:17,799 --> 01:01:21,074
Say hello. This is CEO Han Jeong Yeon of HAN.

523
01:01:24,193 --> 01:01:25,675
Nice to meet you.

524
01:01:25,675 --> 01:01:28,679
Welcome to APPELLO.

525
01:01:39,886 --> 01:01:43,666
Nice to meet you too, CEO Kang.

526
01:02:19,120 --> 01:02:22,002
[#Epilogue]

527
01:02:49,700 --> 01:02:53,016
- Okay, five seconds to go.
- No, three.

528
01:02:53,016 --> 01:02:57,423
Three, two, one!

529
01:03:00,199 --> 01:03:04,426
- I think this form should move over a bit.
- PowerPoint...

530
01:03:04,426 --> 01:03:07,181
- This square is a little...
- It does seem a bit off.

531
01:03:07,181 --> 01:03:09,217
The square is a bit big...

532
01:03:19,609 --> 01:03:22,512
That's basically announcing they're dating.

533
01:03:22,512 --> 01:03:25,060
They say in an office romance,
only the couple doesn't know.

534
01:03:25,060 --> 01:03:27,598
Even the water cooler's in on it.

535
01:03:41,979 --> 01:03:45,504
[Witness 1]

536
01:03:45,504 --> 01:03:48,176
<i>- Let's begin the meeting.
- Yes.</i>

537
01:03:50,563 --> 01:03:52,998
[Seoul Night View Date Spots]

538
01:03:54,842 --> 01:03:56,147
[Witness 2]

539
01:04:00,082 --> 01:04:01,576
[Witness 3]

540
01:04:16,505 --> 01:04:17,517
<i>Da Reum!</i>

541
01:04:17,517 --> 01:04:20,056
<i>Team Lead Kim needs the sample now. Found it?</i>

542
01:04:20,056 --> 01:04:21,161
<i>What? Yes.</i>

543
01:04:21,161 --> 01:04:23,049
<i>Yes, I'll bring it right now!</i>

544
01:04:23,049 --> 01:04:24,559
<i>Yes.</i>

545
01:04:32,271 --> 01:04:34,584
Let's just pretend we don't know for now.

546
01:04:34,584 --> 01:04:37,059
They say they're both beginners at dating.

547
01:04:39,467 --> 01:04:41,041
- Why are you so happy?
- Are you happy?

548
01:04:41,041 --> 01:04:43,744
It's just so exciting.

549
01:04:43,744 --> 01:04:45,529
Have you never dated?

550
01:04:47,296 --> 01:04:48,298
<i>Han Jeong Yeon?</i>

551
01:04:48,298 --> 01:04:49,451
<i>She's Ha Gi's first love.</i>

552
01:04:49,451 --> 01:04:53,550
<i>If you ever make Da Reum cry...</i>

553
01:04:53,550 --> 01:04:55,563
<i>The person who wrote the proposal...</i>

554
01:04:55,563 --> 01:04:58,252
<i>Would you be interested in taking it on?</i>

555
01:04:58,252 --> 01:05:00,169
